        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ursula K. Le Guin\n- Works: The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas, The Day Before the Revolution, The Wind's Twelve Quarters\n- Awards: Hugo Award, Locus Award, Nebula Award\n- Topics: philosophical fiction, short stories\n\nFacts:\n- Ursula K. Le Guin wrote \"The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas,\" a 1973 plotless, short, descriptive work of philosophical fiction that is popularly classified as a short story.\n- \"The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas\" won the Hugo Award in 1974.\n- \"The Day Before the Revolution\" won the Locus Award and the Nebula Award in 1975.\n- The page \"The Wind's Twelve Quarters\" states the awards won by \"The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas\" and \"The Day Before the Revolution.\"",
